{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Now you will see, etc.</b> The reason He said <b>now</b> is a response to what he said: ״And since I came, etc., it has gone worse for Israel״ — more than before. He said to him: <b>now you will see</b> that this evil will soon depart, both the increase and the essence, as indeed it was, for with the first plague of blood the bondage was removed, as our Sages of blessed memory said (Shemot Rabbah 9). And this is the opposite of his thinking, for he thought that the suffering of Israel would persist because of this mission until the time of redemption, as I explained in his words." "<b>Further,</b> it intends to answer him regarding what he said — that the enemy blasphemed HaShem yet He did not show zeal for the honor of His Name — with <b>now you will see what I will do to Pharaoh</b> on this account. And His saying <b>for with a strong hand</b>, etc., will be explained according to one of the reasons we explained, that it was said to Moses [concerning] the plague of the firstborn at the first mission — namely that if Pharaoh had not hardened his face to speak words against the honor of the Blessed One, He would immediately have sent them out with the plague of the firstborn. But because ״he despised the word of YHWH״ (Numbers 15:31), HaShem multiplied His plagues against him. And this is the meaning of His saying <b>for with a strong hand He will send them out</b> — meaning, I will strengthen his heart until I make him taste many bitter and harsh punishments, and only afterward send them out. And this is because he offended the honor of the Most High." "<b>And with a strong hand, etc.</b> Here He informed that HaShem would bring about an earthquake through the infliction of the plague of the firstborn, as our Sages of blessed memory said (Yalkut Shimoni 186) on the verse ״there was no house where there was no dead״ — for the heads of the households died even if there was no firstborn, and firstborn of the father and also firstborn of the mother died. And through this He not only sent them out but expelled them with great haste, as it is written (Exodus 12:33): ״And Egypt pressed, etc., to hasten״, etc. And corresponding to what he said at the beginning: ״Why have you done evil, etc.,״ the answer came in the adjacent section: ״And Elohim spoke, etc.״" "<b>End of parashat Shemot</b>"], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:24:58.176468367Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}